(3171515, 444242, 61413, '<td valign="top">Shouldn''t there be a few more? Or should I count the reflections as well?<br/> <br/>:-)<br/> <br/>On the shot itself, it would have been nice to have been looking at the front of the swans, rather than their backs. a good rule of thumb for nature shots is: if you can see both eyes, then maybe you have the beginnings of a good composition. I''d have cranked the aperture down a little as well - better to be underexposed on the water than over-exposed on your main subject.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps.</td>', 'Shouldn''t there be a few more? Or should I count the reflections as well? :-) On the shot itself, it would have been nice to have been looking at the front of the swans, rather than their backs. a good rule of thumb for nature shots is: if you can see both eyes, then maybe you have the beginnings of a good composition. I''d have cranked the aperture down a little as well - better to be underexposed on the water than over-exposed on your main subject. Hope this helps.', '2007-01-02 16:25:58.000000', NULL, 1),
